{"name":"Toes in the Sand","hex":"#f8dcbf","fetched":"2026-10-13","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"toes","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["plural of toe"]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["third-person singular simple present indicative of toe"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/toes"},{"term":"sand","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Rock that is ground more finely than gravel, but is not as fine as silt (more formally, see grain sizes chart), forming beaches and deserts and also used in construction.\n\n A specific grade, type, or composition of sand.\n\n A beach or other mass of sand.","A specific grade, type, or composition of sand."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of a light beige colour, like that of typical sand."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/sand"}],"entries":[{"title":"Toes in the Sand Recordings","blocks":[{"text":"Toes in the Sand Recordings is a US-based record label founded by David Christopher and Amy Dana in 2004. Specializing in progressive house and progressive breaks, their releases place an emphasis on musicality, arrangement, and composition. Their first release, \"Bound for Ascension\" by Michael Lanning, is featured on Balance 006 [EQ] mixed by Anthony Pappa. Other releases have appeared on compilations by Andrew K, Sprout Music, and more."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toes_in_the_Sand_Recordings"},{"title":"Toe","blocks":[{"text":"Toes are the digits of the foot of a tetrapod. Animal species such as cats that walk on their toes are described as being digitigrade. Humans, and other animals that walk on the soles of their feet, are described as being plantigrade; unguligrade animals are those that walk on hooves at the tips of their toes."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bd/Toes.png/330px-Toes.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Toe"},{"title":"Sand","blocks":[{"text":"Sand is a granular material composed of finely divided mineral particles. Sand has various compositions but is usually defined by its grain size. Sand grains are smaller than gravel and coarser than silt. Sand can also refer to a textural class of soil or soil type; i.e., a soil containing more than 85 percent sand-sized particles by mass."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8b/Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg/330px-Libya_4608_Idehan_Ubari_Dunes_Luca_Galuzzi_2007.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sand"},{"title":"Desert sand (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Desert sand is a very light and very weakly saturated reddish yellow color which corresponds specifically to the coloration of sand. It may also be regarded as a deep tone of beige."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/45/Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG/330px-Sossusvlei_Dune_Namib_Desert_Namibia_Luca_Galuzzi_2004.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Desert_sand_(color)"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Gray269.png/500px-Gray269.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/59/Gray269.png/500px-Gray269.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Bones of the right foot. Plantar surface.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AGray269.png"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Foot_on_white_background_%28cropped%29.jpg/500px-Foot_on_white_background_%28cropped%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/44/Foot_on_white_background_%28cropped%29.jpg/1280px-Foot_on_whit